From 2675a47c1507e855ac8338fedc5721e2c1e57914 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avocado Linux <info@avocadolinux.org>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 20:29:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rzv2n: bl31_platform_setup: settle SoC fabric before TZC/GIC
 init
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

bl31_platform_setup() executes a sequence of MMIO writes to the SoC's
TrustZone Controllers (TZC400 SRAM_0_1 and SRAM_2 instances), GIC
distributor, and bus QoS registers. The upstream tzc400 driver
(drivers/arm/tzc/tzc400.c) does not include barriers, polls, or delays
between disable_filters / configure_region0 / enable_filters; it relies
on the caller to ensure adequate hardware settling time.

At LOG_LEVEL=50, the four INFO() prints inside plat_security_setup
('Configuring TrustZone Controller' x2 + 'Total N regions set.' x2)
clock out roughly 10 ms of UART traffic at 115200 baud between TZC
operations, which happens to be enough settling time for the rzv2n
fabric. At the release-default LOG_LEVEL=20 those prints are compiled
out, the writes proceed back-to-back, and BL31 hangs immediately after
its banner — before any subsequent NOTICE-level output appears.

Add an explicit 10 ms mdelay() at the start of bl31_platform_setup as
the deterministic settling window. Mirrors the analogous fix applied
to xspi_setup() in BL2 for the same root-cause class of races on this
SoC. 10 ms is conservative (real settling time is sub-millisecond on
typical fabric IP) but invisible at boot scale.

Signed-off-by: Avocado Linux <info@avocadolinux.org>
Signed-off-by: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
---
 plat/renesas/rz/soc/v2n/bl31_plat_setup.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/renesas/rz/soc/v2n/bl31_plat_setup.c b/plat/renesas/rz/soc/v2n/bl31_plat_setup.c
index f5b130f08..562d6f4df 100644
--- a/plat/renesas/rz/soc/v2n/bl31_plat_setup.c
+++ b/plat/renesas/rz/soc/v2n/bl31_plat_setup.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <rz_private.h>
 #include <rz_soc_def.h>
 #include <pwrc.h>
+#include <drivers/delay_timer.h>
 #include <drivers/generic_delay_timer.h>
 #include <syc.h>
 
@@ -115,6 +116,19 @@ void bl31_plat_arch_setup(void)
 
 void bl31_platform_setup(void)
 {
+	/*
+	 * Settling delay before touching SoC bus interconnect / TZC / GIC.
+	 * The release-default LOG_LEVEL=20 build hangs in this function on
+	 * rzv2n-sr-som; LOG_LEVEL=50 boots through because the ~10 ms of
+	 * incidental UART traffic from plat_security_setup's INFO prints
+	 * provides settling time the upstream tzc400 driver lacks (no
+	 * barriers/polls between disable_filters / configure / enable_filters).
+	 * 10 ms here is the same conservative value used to fix the analogous
+	 * BL2 xspi_setup race; far longer than the actual hardware needs but
+	 * dwarfed by overall boot time.
+	 */
+	mdelay(10);
+
 	plat_security_setup();
 
 	/* initialize GIC-600 */
-- 
2.53.0

